{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,30]],"date-time":"2026-03-30T06:15:07Z","timestamp":1774851307458,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":8,"publisher":"American Astronomical Society","issue":"3","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,27]],"date-time":"2026-03-27T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1774569600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,27]],"date-time":"2026-03-27T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1774569600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/iopscience.iop.org\/info\/page\/text-and-data-mining"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["iopscience.iop.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Res. Notes AAS"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,27]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    The Quick-Look Pipeline (QLP; C. X. Huang et al. 2020; M. Kunimoto et al. 2021, and references therein) generates light curves for up to 2 million stars every 27.4 days observed by TESS as part of its planet search. As machine learning methods enable deeper searches and scientific priorities shift toward fainter stars, there is a motivation for QLP to perform better at fainter magnitudes. We have adopted the photometry methods employed by the TESS-Gaia Light Curve package, which has been shown to have better noise characteristics than the original QLP photometry from 10.5 &lt;\n                    <jats:italic>T<\/jats:italic>\n                    &lt; 13.5. We still perform aperture photometry and deliver 3 apertures, and 3 levels of detrending for all stars brighter than\n                    <jats:italic>T<\/jats:italic>\n                    = 13.5, so the changes should be seamless for external users. This method is implemented as of Sector 94 in QLP light curves and is providing users with higher precision light curves and allows detection of fainter signals in our planet searches.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3847\/2515-5172\/ae5790","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,30]],"date-time":"2026-03-30T04:51:31Z","timestamp":1774846291000},"page":"69","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["QLP Data Release Notes 004: TESS-Gaia Light Curve Photometry Implementation"],"prefix":"10.3847","volume":"10","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0005-2122-0680","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Glen","family":"Petitpas","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0005-3397-2046","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Jack","family":"Haviland","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7127-7643","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Te","family":"Han","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0241-2757","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Willie","family":"Fong","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2135-9018","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Katharine","family":"Hesse","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1836-3120","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Avi","family":"Shporer","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4371-3460","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Jeroen","family":"Audenaert","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5788-9280",